the latest on the tragedy at a houston  concert that killed eight people rapper  travis scott continued to perform after  the declaration of a mass casualty event  the city's police chief had initially  defended his decision not to stop the  show immediately but yesterday he told a  different story lilia luciano has more  for roughly an hour a chaotic scene  raged at the astroworld music festival  friday night and the show continued for  almost 40 minutes after a mass casualty  event was declared now investigators are  trying to figure out why on wednesday  houston police chief troy finner said  his officers were in communication with  festival personnel the cpr was being  administered to multiple individuals he  later clarified on twitter that police  also told those in charge of the event  to shut down the performance the  ultimate authority to end the show is  with production  and the entertainer okay and that should  be through communication with  public service safety officials but on  saturday in the more immediate aftermath  of the festival finner defended the  decision to let the show continue and  said his department was part of that  choice  you cannot just close when you got 50  000 and over 50 000 individuals okay we  have to worry about riding and there was  a cooperation and discussion between  promoters  my fire department the police department  so i i think that part was was pretty  good  cbs news obtained video from a source  close to the astroworld music festival  appearing to show police near the stage  during scott's performance this video  was shot at around 10 pm with police  seemingly unaware of the severity of the  situation in the crowd some 20 minutes  after the mass casualty event was  declared the source says that means it  would be difficult for the performers to  know as well  we've reached out to the houston police  department for comment about those  images in the timeline and are yet to  hear back but late wednesday night  travis scott's attorney put out a  statement accusing city officials of  finger-pointing of sending inconsistent  messages and on backtracking from their  original statements gail  still a lot of questions there thank you  very much lilia
 

